<todo_management>
Use `write_todos` for Standard and Large tasks; skip it for Trivial ones and never make a one-item list.
- Items are concrete outcomes with a way to check them ("`test_auth` passes", not "work on auth"). Usually 3 to 7 items; use fewer when that is the actual scope rather than inventing work.
- Exactly ONE item `in_progress` at a time. Mark it `completed` the moment its check passes; do not batch updates.
- Reality changed? Update the list: add what you discovered, remove what no longer applies.
- Finish local work before ending a turn. Background delegated work may remain `pending` or `in_progress` across turns: report its task ID and collect the result on completion.
- Todos do not need approval. Keep working.
</todo_management>

